  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Ul'nigid' was published by the Women's Studio Workshop (WSW) in Rosendale, NY. ... The image and title were printed with polymer plates on Colophon and handmade paper. The text was letterpress printed in 12 Bembo italic and 24 point Cherokee Syllabary"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Ul'nigid' was made to honor the artist's Grandmother, Martha Reed-Bark. This moveable book structure is able to take on multiple renderings, and utilizes letterpress printing with Cherokee syllabary metal type and weaving processes similar to those of a traditional Cherokee white oak basket"--Publisher's description.</subfield>
